---
/**
 * The scene slot, shown in full (animated) mode only.
 *
 * Every page is built in fallback mode (`data-render-mode="fallback"` on <html>, set in
 * BaseLayout). public/render-mode.js, a classic script in <head>, switches to `full` before the
 * first paint when every check of `chooseRenderMode()` (src/lib/render-mode.ts) passes; a unit
 * test keeps the two in step. No JavaScript or a script error leaves a working fallback page.
 *
 * The scene slot holds the page's animated scene, passed in as the default slot: on the home
 * pages Kálmán following the dive (DivePage.astro), elsewhere nothing. It is decorative only,
 * so it is hidden from screen readers; all content stays in the HTML around it.
 */
---

<div class="scene-slot" data-scene-slot aria-hidden="true">
  <slot />
</div>

<style>
  /* In fallback mode the slot takes no space; the animated scene only appears in full mode. */
  :global(html[data-render-mode='fallback']) .scene-slot {
    display: none;
  }
</style>
